Z||000011||DaRkLoRD||09-20-2000||02:23 PM||||There were 2 Fiero kits with that name.. one was a Russian kit, the other was a Testarossa lookalike, made in the USA.<P>which one are you referring to? TR makes me suspect it's the ferrari lookalike.. which was ok, but nothing compared to the russian pyranha.. but if it is the russian kit.. GO FOR IT ARCHIE!!!!!<P>But then I'd have a major dilemma.... get a Finale or get a Pyranha.  (minus the huge wing of course)  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||4
Z||000012||KitKar||09-20-2000||03:09 PM||||I think it would be great if it was reproduced. But, at a reasonable price like PISA's kits. Personally I think the Finale is overpriced otherwise I would get one. Now I am looking at an Artero.<P>------------------<BR>Rick Lord<BR>Webmaster<BR>http://www.KitKar.com||||reg||1
Z||000013||Archie||09-20-2000||09:36 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by DaRkLoRD:<BR><B>There were 2 Fiero kits with that name.. one was a Russian kit, the other was a Testarossa lookalike, made in the USA.<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>The TR Piranha was originally brought to kit car form by Tom H. At Pacific Motorsports in Anihiem, CA., it was a Kenny Youngblood design and was features in the "Action Jackson" movie. Pacific sold the tooling to Pete Hoffman in Harrisburg, PA in like 1990. Pete sold the molds to GlassTech in Harveysburg, OH in 1994 (I think). GlassTech was owned by the late Bill Keller, he sold the business just before his untimely demise last year to a "non-Kit Car" type guy. The molds are lying unused in Harveysburg right now.<P>This is the car that looks a bit like the T.R. and not the Russian car.<P>There has only been one of the Russian style Piranha's ever built. It is my assumption, based on the Russian's car's rarity and on what was said that Fiero86 has one of the TR Piranha's.<P>Hope this helps.<P>Archie<BR>(maker of the overpriced Fino & Finale kits) ||||reg||1
Z||000014||V8Fiero||09-20-2000||10:38 PM||||If Im not mistaken, I beleive there is one on sale on ebay right now. Anyway he says the thing about "Action Jackson"||||reg||1
Z||000015||DaRkLoRD||09-21-2000||10:34 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Archie:<BR><B>There has only been one of the Russian style Piranha's ever built.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I've seen 2 different pyranha interiors, but only one exterior.. (as far as I know.. they might just both have been red) so I assumed there were at least 2 prototypes out there.<P> <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR><B><BR>Archie<BR>(maker of the overpriced Fino & Finale kits) </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>LOL.. somehow I expected you'd mention that sooner or later, after the above comment.. personally, the Finale kit is out of my price range at the moment.. but I don't think the pricing is out of line, especially compared to the cost of some lambo and ferrari kits.. not to mention the fact that the Finale is so much cooler looking than most other rebodies, and it's original too.. not a copy of a production car.. and someday I'll get one... someday.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <A HREF="mailto:steve@fieroproject.com">steve@fieroproject.com</A>  <BR><A HREF="http://www.fieroproject.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fieroproject.com</A>||||reg||1
